# pattern:location — why it's intentional (and what would reverse it)
# Reviewed 2026-07-28, standard depth × changed scope (delta since v1.12.36).

blind-except:empirica/core/redaction.py:140 — fails CLOSED (emits the placeholder, never raw text). A redactor that degrades to pass-through is worse than none because callers believe they are protected. Reverse if it ever returns the input on error.
blind-except:empirica/core/version_drift.py:75,103,129 — best-effort by contract; a drift check must never crash a long-running daemon. Safe direction verified: if the distribution cannot be resolved, version_drift() also returns None, so no self-exit is triggered. Reverse if a caller starts treating None as "confirmed no drift" rather than "no signal".
blind-except:empirica/core/loop_scheduler/persistent_listener.py:116,461,510 — pre-existing, unchanged by this delta.
complexity:empirica/plugins/.../sentinel-gate.py::_validate_check_record D(29) — pre-existing, untouched. Functions added in this delta are A/B (worst B(9)).
complexity:empirica/core/qdrant/memory.py::search C(16) — pre-existing shape; this delta REDUCED branching by collapsing focused/all into one branch.

# Reviewed 2026-08-01, deep depth × repo scope (pre-release sweep for 1.13.0).
blind-except:empirica/core/cockpit/loop_registry.py:120,415,527 — narrow typed catches (FileNotFoundError/OSError) around optional state-file reads, not blind swallows. Absence of the file is the normal case. Reverse if the catch widens to Exception.
blind-except:empirica/core/qdrant/pattern_retrieval.py:861 — narrow (TypeError/ValueError) around per-item score coercion inside a loop; skipping one malformed payload is correct and the alternative is dropping the whole result set. Pre-existing (7a7a7aa30, 2026-07-10).
complexity:empirica/core/cockpit/canonical_loops.py::maybe_queue_canonical_install C — a documented 5-gate cascade (project / stamp / registry / opt_in_only / kind==cron). The branching IS the specification; flattening it would hide the gates. Reverse if a sixth gate lands without a matching test.
semantic-drift:empirica/plugins/claude-code-integration/scripts/statusline_empirica.py::_cwd_project_root — requires sessions.db as well as project.yaml, where session_resolver's cwd guards need only project.yaml. Two questions, not drift: the statusline opens <root>/.empirica/sessions/sessions.db directly, so a root with no local store cannot answer for it, and following the cwd there would create a stray store. Same reason as path_resolver._try_context_project_db. Reverse if the statusline starts honouring EMPIRICA_SESSION_DB or stops opening the store by path. (Flagged by the pre-1.14.1 sweep, judged by design 2026-09-25.)
silent-return:empirica/core/cockpit/{liveness.py::_process_alive,launcher/state.py::pid_alive,instance_actions.py::_process_alive} — PermissionError from os.kill(pid, 0) returns False ("dead"). By design: these probe OUR processes, and a PID now owned by another user is the PID-reuse case, so our process is gone. Reverse if any caller starts probing processes it does not own. (Silent-handlers census 2026-09-25.)
silent-return:empirica/cli/command_handlers/auth_commands.py::_verify_token — any HTTPError returns False, so a 5xx reads like a rejected token. Fails safe: the only consequence is "do not retire this seat's api_key". Reverse if False ever gates something destructive. (Census 2026-09-25.)
silent-return:empirica/cli/command_handlers/_workflow_shared.py::_read_project_gate_scalars — {} on any error, so a corrupt project.yaml falls back to default gate scalars. Documented, and the corrupt file is now reported at session-create (project_root_warning, 680edd00f). Reverse if a practice's enforcement depends on this block with no other signal. (Census 2026-09-25.)
